decisions:
  - id: D-auto-graph-default-on
    decision: Auto-graph generation defaults to true
    rationale: 'Graph should always be current — users who don''t want it can set graph.auto-generate: false in config'
  - id: D-sweep-fix-default
    decision: Sweep auto-fix is ON by default
    rationale: Sweep is a maintenance action — if you're running it, you want cleanup. --dry for preview.
  - id: D-heatmap-local-types
    decision: Heat map and pipeline MCP tools define types locally instead of importing from CLI package
    rationale: CLI and MCP are separate tsup build targets — cross-package imports would break the build
  - id: D-tier-thresholds
    decision: Hot threshold 15, warm threshold 5 for tier classification
    rationale: Conservative defaults that can be tuned via context.tiers in config.yaml
  - id: D-pipeline-templates
    decision: '4 built-in pipeline templates: add-feature, bug-fix, security-change, refactor'
    rationale: Cover 90% of use cases while allowing custom --gates override
learnings:
  - Parallel builder agents work well for independent features — 4 agents built 4 features concurrently with zero conflicts
  - Doctor refactor from single file to directory was smooth — test imports updated, shift.ts import updated
  - Pre-existing test failures (hooks, integration-build) should not block feature development — our changes actually reduced failures by 1
  - Heat map confidence decay (5% per 30 days) prevents stale lock-in while being conservative enough to retain useful associations
